#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119550 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "b25256b2-09fe-5faa-b27a-bfea7654e8ef" :question/math-academy-id "e-3019" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} [  3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) ] \\,\\textrm{d}t$ given that $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2} \\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 16, \\: 2,\\: -2\\right\\rangle$ and $\\displaystyle{\\int_0^2}\\mathbf g(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 2,-4,2\\right\\rangle .$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\big[ \\, 3 \\mathbf f(t)+\\mathbf g(t) \\, \\big] \\, \\textrm d t =  \\displaystyle {3\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t + \\displaystyle {\\int_0^2 } \\mathbf g(t) \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[3f(t)+g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨16,\\,2,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨48,\\,6,\\,-6⟩+⟨2,\\,-4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨50,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119551 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "5c4164d7-605a-597c-9bab-f6599becc527" :question/math-academy-id "e-3020" :question/problem "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle \\dfrac{3}{2}, \\: 1, \\: 3 \\right\\rangle$\nand\n$\\displaystyle\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\left\\langle 0, \\: 2, \\: 6 \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t=\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t+\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n\\int_{-1}^0\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t = \n\\int_{-1}^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t - \\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2,\\,6⟩-⟨\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,1,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119552 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "1d356bbb-b4ad-5730-9bd1-7f3cd151f96f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3021" :question/problem "Find $\\displaystyle {\\int_0^1 }  \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t)  \\, \\textrm d t$ \ngiven that \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1\\mathbf f(t)\\,\\textrm d t = \\mathbf i-3\\,\\mathbf j-4\\,\\mathbf k$ \nand \n$\\mathbf c=\\mathbf j-\\mathbf k .$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf c \\times \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t =  \\mathbf c \\times {\\int_0^1 } \\mathbf f(t) \\, \\textrm d t  .\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(j-k)\\times (i-3\\,j-4\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(-4-3)i-(0+1)j+(0-1)k \\\\  & =-7\\,i-\\,j-\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119698 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/id #uuid "40927582-03c4-5dcb-b2cc-7c68c73388b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8688" :question/problem "Calculate \n$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2\\mathbf f(t) + \\langle 1,\\:-1,\\:1\\rangle\\,\\textrm{d}t$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle\\int_2^0\\mathbf f(t) \\,\\textrm{d}t= \\left\\langle -3, \\: 2, \\: 1 \\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨t,\\,-t,\\,t⟩{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,-1⟩+⟨2,\\,-2,\\,2⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,-4,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262951 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0549aad0-d3df-5bda-b5ff-a2a28949ce32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-8,\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259920} {:answer/id #uuid "9a34877b-0c90-54bc-a15c-e4ef580ff774" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1,\\,2,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261212} {:answer/id #uuid "9fbe6911-5632-5913-a554-2c6c9b2cd4ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-10,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261260} {:answer/id #uuid "a9dcd6b2-1af9-52b2-863a-f10202e72cc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-6,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261361} {:answer/id #uuid "ad108365-5066-5f63-ba54-eb2a13ec2de6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-5,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fbe6911-5632-5913-a554-2c6c9b2cd4ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-10,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261260} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e799d64-76f3-5753-a340-9612a01bb001" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "595f95a8-e242-59b0-85cf-ad884a52eaa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-129140" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩$\nand \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=3{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩-⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,-6,\\,3⟩-⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-10,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119980 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0333b70a-2ede-5c8d-b298-4d25ae4d4667" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Vector Addition and Scalar Multiplication Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afc8add8-a972-543e-ba5d-502649377eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,2\\sqrt{2}+1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388001} {:answer/id #uuid "88d76c60-f635-5b53-b9a2-21eb7b22c38d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-5,\\,\\sqrt{2}-2,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388002} {:answer/id #uuid "c6d13bc7-8fd9-5c74-85e1-35ca1c16399f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,\\,2\\sqrt{2}-6,\\,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388003} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f9b0d5-b1ef-500e-9a9a-1756568b9eee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6,\\,5\\sqrt{2}+1,\\,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388004} {:answer/id #uuid "a27359af-1ebf-57f7-a5f2-e6e3c036c4a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,2\\sqrt{2}-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a27359af-1ebf-57f7-a5f2-e6e3c036c4a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-12,\\,2\\sqrt{2}-1,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388005} :answer-field/id #uuid "08002127-d475-5849-b316-13394942fb74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "57f0244e-104a-5517-a9c5-a53620a2a15d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129149" :question/problem "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{3}[2f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-3,\\,\\sqrt{2},\\,2⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{4},\\,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}[2f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=2{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[2f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =2{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2⟨-3,\\,\\sqrt{2},\\,2⟩+4⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{4},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,\\,2\\sqrt{2},\\,4⟩+⟨-6,\\,-1,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-12,\\,2\\sqrt{2}-1,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02719984-1eed-5b45-abb8-f9d57dc603d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-13,\\,-5,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263020} {:answer/id #uuid "860b18bb-4f4a-53c7-963e-483683ca820f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,\\,-8,\\,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264156} {:answer/id #uuid "ac417052-a513-5339-871c-05eea4809c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,\\,-10,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264479} {:answer/id #uuid "e01c6d3f-0fda-5f52-8740-cb7b48f432c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨15,\\,-2,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264946} {:answer/id #uuid "ef1f1b37-f089-50aa-ae75-d977544c3e4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9,\\,-12,\\,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac417052-a513-5339-871c-05eea4809c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-9,\\,-10,\\,8⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264479} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5a9a315-8af0-5512-bbf8-ebf3e0bd6e5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265651}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "620fd628-6fe2-5040-9cd0-aaf37f31206b" :question/math-academy-id "q-129268" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{4}^{0}f(t)+⟨3,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-3,\\,6,\\,0⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,6,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-6,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{0}f(t)+⟨3,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{4}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{4}^{0}⟨3,\\,1,\\,-2⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-6,\\,0⟩+⟨3t,\\,t,\\,-2t⟩{|}_{4}^{0} \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-6,\\,0⟩+⟨-12,\\,-4,\\,8⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨-9,\\,-10,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c08ea4b-77bf-5be9-95f7-6f7a1369c182" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\,i+2\\,j-k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263656} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffc9ed7-eb98-5a8d-b53f-7bb55b6b45aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,i-5\\,j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263830} {:answer/id #uuid "bd254509-fcff-5a01-9878-c181c3cd57fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+3\\,j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264642} {:answer/id #uuid "be01fa84-fad6-5ae4-9c1e-a73ae3b28a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-i+5\\,j+k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264651} {:answer/id #uuid "ef1adc9e-0280-54e8-ab23-e88e4d69a7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+5\\,j+2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef1adc9e-0280-54e8-ab23-e88e4d69a7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+5\\,j+2\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265096} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7c3c66d-9b18-5c7a-bf81-ae419bdf2386" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265597}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "553c9eff-921e-5636-9757-6a75aa064098" :question/math-academy-id "q-129295" :question/problem "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=i+j-3\\,k$ \nand \n$c=i-j+2\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i-j+2\\,k)\\times (i+j-3\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-2)i-(-3-2)j+(1+1)k \\\\  & =i+5\\,j+2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120181 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119982 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c8ee97e-f2b0-587e-9171-8008f1e0c4aa" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Product Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9576cb80-15e0-5b18-83aa-0eeef843ebeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i + 2j - 24k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117248} {:answer/id #uuid "acd690cf-8194-5e19-a5e8-82a898cb76b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i - 2j + 8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117249} {:answer/id #uuid "ea405287-6d2d-5b0f-ad31-56a4d68a2c83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i + 2j - 8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117250} {:answer/id #uuid "ef9c86b6-fb7c-5beb-a2cd-bab10b1ba048" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i + 2j + 8k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117251} {:answer/id #uuid "6de54278-69ce-5bb5-9441-bf179daf9e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i + 2j + 24k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117252}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ac63dd9f-32cd-5ec8-8fb2-52c021ed5db9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117247}] :question/id #uuid "e79507a4-566e-5fff-acc4-da31b5f94ddb" :question/math-academy-id "q-32521" :question/problem "Find $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2}c \\cdot f(t)dt$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2}f(t)dt = 16i + 8j + 2k$\nand\n$c =-i + j$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119981 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d5287f63-6d1a-5710-8a71-df5d1ba09a00" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Adjacent Intervals Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46bf7675-80a2-559b-8162-709a1a0d7f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨10,\\,6,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358358} {:answer/id #uuid "52b55dd5-256e-5209-86de-a9c9700d2990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨7,\\,2,\\,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358461} {:answer/id #uuid "90b044f6-737d-5f41-adc8-0bdca392f181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359017} {:answer/id #uuid "e6dcc4aa-84e5-52fb-b4ea-896d476393a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9,\\,1,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359794} {:answer/id #uuid "ec412725-0d94-59a0-8fbf-bf17919c936a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,-3,\\,11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90b044f6-737d-5f41-adc8-0bdca392f181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359017} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3e28b5a-b897-5ddd-a2bd-d85b9a72bf4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29982efe-8588-56f9-8a2e-657a512dab79" :question/math-academy-id "q-96943" :question/problem "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,3,\\,4⟩-⟨8,\\,-6,\\,15⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-10,\\,9,\\,-11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120556 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eb7fd4f-f4bc-535e-b6bf-0c7df387a375" :knowledge-point/title "Reversing the Limits of Integration"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "975116c1-faed-520f-9445-82138e386d23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3, 2,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119450} {:answer/id #uuid "9b08ef23-6ce5-5657-a87b-1da31d040bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-2,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119451} {:answer/id #uuid "a840ca18-9476-5370-9927-9e4dba429afb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4, 1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119452} {:answer/id #uuid "e3648bbf-605d-503c-a43a-7e2b910b557d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4, 1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119453} {:answer/id #uuid "5f730c2a-84ac-543c-b6f5-7651ef6c69d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,-2, 1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119454}] :answer-field/id #uuid "114f26d7-6c07-5fb1-aa45-8dac954ec030" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119449}] :question/id #uuid "63279440-ddaa-5ce9-9454-481ab5b36e09" :question/math-academy-id "q-98093" :question/problem "Calculate\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{1}f(t) + ⟨1, 1, 1⟩dt$\ngiven that\n$\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{0}f(t)dt = ⟨ - 2, 3, 4⟩$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119879 :knowledg